Not taken: every other file of test/clojure/test_clojure/. The rule and the per-file reasons are in
docs/notes/corpus.md, "Clojure's own suite: what is in and what is out".

shim/ is ours, not Clojure's: stand-ins for the support namespaces the files require and the JVM test
tooling supplies (clojure.data.generators, clojure.test.generative, clojure.test.check and
clojure.test.check.*, Clojure's own test_clojure/generators.clj) plus an empty
clojure.test-clojure.protocols, so a file's own (ns ...) form loads instead of taking the whole file
down with it. Each shim file says what it stands in for.
